Debian PyArrow package for Qore gRPC qualification
=================================================

Copyright 2026 Qore Technologies, s.r.o.

Prepare this source with tools/prepare-debian-backports.py --suite trixie.
The manifest pins the upstream PyPI source distribution by URL and SHA-256.
The package builds offline through PEP 517 with Debian build dependencies,
including the separately qualified Cython backport and Apache's Arrow 25
library packages. No wheel or Arrow C++ library is downloaded during the build.

The recipe retains the upstream private libarrow_python bridge libraries and
their $ORIGIN runtime search path inside the Python package. They are not a
public C++ ABI and do not replace the system Arrow libraries. Debian's compiler
flags, hardening, automatic debug symbols and normal debhelper stripping apply.
The CMake build directory stays below the source root so Debian's prefix maps
also cover generated Cython C++ files and their debug information.

The libcst build requirement is removed because upstream 25.0.1 disables the
only feature that uses it: extracting docstrings for the unfinished type stubs.
The patch does not disable any enabled upstream feature or runtime test.

Array, compute, IPC, Acero, dataset, Parquet and loopback Flight checks run
during the build and against the installed package. They are bounded, offline
public API checks, not a claim that the full upstream suite has been run.
CUDA, Gandiva, Substrait, ORC, HDFS, Parquet encryption and cloud integrations
are outside this recipe's feature scope.

Native amd64 and arm64 qualification, source/binary reproducibility, package
lifecycle checks and downstream Flight interoperability must pass before
publication. These recipes alone do not establish release qualification.
